' core-health is deliberately not included here: it's a standalone,
' always-on RabbitMQ/Redis monitor that polls the broker and Redis on its
' own connections and republishes telemetry — it never sits in the
' message's own path (receiver -> message-processor -> archive-processor ->
' archive-compaction -> S3) the way this diagram depicts, so it has no
' natural home in a linear pipeline view. See core-health/README.md and
' issue #1867.
title Message Pipeline

!includesub ../../../receiver/receiver.puml!COMPONENT
!includesub ../../../message-processor/message-processor.puml!COMPONENT
!includesub central-server.puml!COMPONENT
!includesub ../../../archive-processor/archive-processor.puml!COMPONENT
!includesub ../../../archive-compaction/archive-compaction.puml!COMPONENT
!includesub aws.puml!COMPONENT

Receiver -> adsbx : Publisher
ProcessorC ----> adsbq : Consumer
ProcessorC -down--> Redis : Enrichment lookups
ProcessorC --> archiveq : Publisher
Archiver -up-> archiveq : Consumer
Archiver ---> s3 : Persist flight\n(flights/{YYYY}/{MM}/{DD}/{uuid}.json.gz)
Archiver ---> s3 : Persist Parquet index row\n(index/year={YYYY}/month={MM}/day={DD}/{uuid}.parquet)
Compactor ---> s3 : Read + merge a day's small Parquet files,\nwrite one compacted file
Compactor ---> s3 : Delete compacted sources

RevProc -[hidden]down-> MsgProc
MsgProc -[hidden]down-> CentralSvr
CentralSvr -[hidden]down-> ArchProc
ArchProc -[hidden]down---> AWS
ArchProc -[hidden]right-> ArchCompaction

@enduml
